#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:15
msgid "Test Runner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:17
msgid ""
"**PlatformIO Test Runner** is a powerful unit testing tool. It runs your "
"unit tests located in the :ref:`projectconf_pio_test_dir`, navigates through "
"tests, and facilitates the processing of test results. Test Runner supports "
"the most popular :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:22
msgid ""
"Test Runner allows you to run specific project environments or filter tests "
"using the \"Glob patterns\". Once tests are finished, Test Runner provides a "
"rich report with the status of all test suites and test cases (passed, "
"failed, ignored/skipped)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:31
msgid "Local Test Runner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:33
msgid ""
"**Local Test Runner** allows you to run a test on a local host machine or on "
"a local target device (board). In this case, you need to use the :ref:"
"`cmd_test` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:40
msgid "Remote Test Runner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:42
msgid ""
"**Remote Test Runner** allows you to run test on the remote machine or on "
"the remote target device (board) without having to depend on OS software, "
"extra software, SSH, VPN or opening network ports. Remote Unit Testing works "
"in pair with :ref:`pioremote`. In this case, you need to use the special "
"command :ref:`cmd_remote_test`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:48
msgid ""
"PlatformIO supports multiple :ref:`ci` systems where you can run unit tests "
"at each integration stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:54
msgid "Test Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:56
msgid ""
"Before writing a test, you need to decide where it will be executed later: "
"on the host machine or on the target device connected to the host machine. "
"Tests that are written for the target device typically will not work on your "
"host machine due to the missing peripheral and other connectivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:61
msgid ""
"Using the :ref:`unit_testing_test_hierarchy` allows you to organize tests by "
"types and later skip an incompatible group of tests using :ref:"
"`projectconf_test_filter` or :ref:`projectconf_test_ignore` options in :ref:"
"`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:67
msgid "Native"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:69
msgid ""
"Native tests are intended for the project components that are independent of "
"physical hardware. You can also use them in pair with Mocking frameworks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:72
msgid ""
"PlatformIO provides you a :ref:`platform_native` development platform to "
"build and run tests on the local host machine or using :ref:`ci` VM instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:77
msgid ""
"PlatformIO does not install automatically any toolchains for the :ref:"
"`platform_native` development platform. It depends on the system ``GCC`` "
"toolchain that must be added to the ``PATH`` system environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:82
msgid ""
"Please check the \"Installation\" guide for the :ref:`platform_native` "
"development platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:86
msgid "Embedded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:88
msgid ""
"Embedded tests are intended for the target devices (boards, hardware). They "
"allow you to deeply test all project components that are part of your "
"firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:91
msgid "How does PlatformIO Unit Testing Runner process embedded tests?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:93
msgid ""
"It builds a special firmware intended for your target using a compatible "
"embedded development platform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:95
msgid "Uploads a firmware to the end target (flashes device)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:96
msgid ""
"Connects to the target using a Serial interface and :ref:"
"`projectconf_test_port`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:97
msgid ""
"Gathers Serial output from the target and parses test result on the host "
"machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:99
msgid "Provides test results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:101
msgid ""
"Please check :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks` documentation and learn how to "
"provide a custom configuration or to get full control of PlatformIO Unit "
"Testing Runner using :ref:`unit_testing_frameworks_custom` implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:107
msgid "Hybrid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/unit-testing/runner.rst:109
msgid ""
"The tests that work on a host machine and on the embedded target are hybrid "
"tests. You can run them using :ref:`platform_native` development platform or "
"embedded development :ref:`platforms`."
msgstr ""
